Lightning SPP — Component-based licensing
Policy recorded on 11 October 2026

MIT SDK and clients; commercial engine and runtime.
This is a component split, not a choice of MIT for the entire product.

1. MIT components
The original project files under the following directories are covered by the
full MIT License in LICENSE-MIT.txt:
  SDK/                  SDK interfaces and convenience entry points
  Examples/             integration and usage examples
  Desktop/              Windows desktop client
  VSExtension/          Visual Studio client integration
  Web/wwwroot/          original browser-client code and public static content

Dependencies and third-party material retain their own licenses. The MIT grant
for these components does not grant rights to commercial components they call.

2. Commercial components
Other original project components, including the processing engine, Services/,
Documents/, Configuration/, Licensing/, the server-side Web/ files,
Persistence/Longo/, and root runtime/API entry points are covered by
LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.txt. Their commercial use and redistribution require an
applicable written agreement with the authorized licensor.

The current LightningSPP package and application contain both MIT and commercial
components. They must not be represented as an MIT-only engine distribution.

3. Existing grants and third-party rights
This policy does not revoke rights already granted under MIT for earlier copies
or versions. The repository history retains the license notices for those
versions. Existing MIT grants remain applicable to the code covered by them;
this policy must not be used to claim that previously MIT-licensed code has
become exclusively proprietary. Third-party copyrights and licenses remain
unchanged. Contributors must have authority to license their contributions.

Contact for commercial agreements: ABA GmbH, clisonix@pm.me.
